#### 2. Get Status (GET to `/status`)

**A. Get All Records (JSON default):**
```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:5000/status

**B. Get All Running Hosts (Text output):**
```bash
curl "http://127.0.0.1:5000/status?status=running&output=text"

**C. Get Specific Hostname (JSON):**
```bash
curl "http://127.0.0.1:5000/status?hostname=db-prod-02"

**D. Get Hosts with Wildcard (Raw/CSV output):**
```bash
# Finds hosts starting with 'web' (like 'webserver-01')
curl "http://127.0.0.1:5000/status?hostname=web*&output=raw"

#### 3. Delete Records (DELETE to `/records`)

**A. Delete All Error Records:**
```bash
curl -X DELETE "http://127.0.0.1:5000/records?status=error"

**B. Delete a Specific Host:**
```bash
curl -X DELETE "http://127.0.0.1:5000/records?hostname=db-prod-02"

**C. Delete All Records (No filters):**
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:5000/records

